 "geometry_basis": "Proposal, not the built stadium. The winning competition entry (10 A0 boards published as 150 dpi images) is the only design source. Plan position and axis come from georeferencing its 1:1000 site plans against Overture footprints (about 2 m / 0.3 degree uncertainty). Plan dimensions come from its 1:500 floor plans calibrated on the 105 x 68 m pitch; long-stand heights from the 1:200 characteristic section; end-stand heights from the 1:500 long section and elevations. The sheets disagree by a few metres; plans were preferred for plan positions and the 1:200 section for the long-stand profile. Facade ribs, door positions, vomitories, aisle spacing, roof panelling, fins, trusses and floodlights are drawn from the renders at approximate spacing. Interiors are not modelled beyond the visible hospitality glazing. The modelled seat count is an estimate from the drawn tiers, not the brief's certified 35,000. Pitch level 118.0 m a.s.l. is the competition programme's value for the existing pitch; the forecourt is modelled at +1.8 m as drawn. It replaces the existing stadium's GDI, DGU and Overture parts in the apps at the user's request (2026-09-25). Because Station3D does not carve terrain under landmark meshes, the pitch surface is modelled at +0.5 m (118.5 m) and the forecourt on one plane, +2.05 m on the halfway line falling 0.5 % to the south, so both clear every 1 m DMR cell by at least 0.21 m; the section's forecourt is +1.8 m and the brief's pitch 118.0 m.",
